# React Component Patterns

## Component Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks (no class components)
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)
- Prefer composition over prop drilling
- Use Context sparingly (only for truly global state)
- Memoize expensive calculations with `useMemo`
- Memoize callbacks with `useCallback` when needed

## Props
- Destructure props in function signature
- Use TypeScript interfaces for prop types
- Make optional props explicit with `?`
- Provide sensible defaults using default parameters

Example:
```typescript
interface CardProps {
  title: string
  description?: string
  onClick?: () => void
  className?: string
}

export function Card({
  title,
  description = "No description provided",
  onClick,
  className,
}: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("card", className)} onClick={onClick}>
      <h3>{title}</h3>
      <p>{description}</p>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## State Management
- Use `useState` for local component state
- Use `useReducer` for complex state logic
- Keep state as local as possible (lift only when needed)
- Use React Query (TanStack Query) for server state

Example:
```typescript
// Local state
const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false)

// Complex state
const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducer, initialState)

// Server state
const { data, isLoading } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["capabilities"],
  queryFn: getCapabilities,
})
```

## Hooks
- Place hooks at the top of the component
- Follow the order: state hooks, effect hooks, custom hooks
- Don't call hooks conditionally
- Create custom hooks for reusable logic (prefix with `use`)

Example:
```typescript
export function useCapabilityTracking(capabilityId: string) {
  const [isTracking, setIsTracking] = useState(false)

  const { mutate: toggleTracking } = useMutation({
    mutationFn: () => toggleCapabilityTracking(capabilityId),
    onSuccess: () => setIsTracking(prev => !prev),
  })

  return { isTracking, toggleTracking }
}
```

## React Query (TanStack Query)
- Use for client-side server state caching
- Use `useQuery` for GET operations
- Use `useMutation` for mutations
- Implement optimistic updates
- Set appropriate cache times

Example:
```typescript
import { useQuery, useMutation, useQueryClient } from "@tanstack/react-query"

export function CapabilitiesList() {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient()

  const { data, isLoading } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ["capabilities"],
    queryFn: getCapabilities,
  })

  const { mutate: trackCapability } = useMutation({
    mutationFn: (id: string) => trackCapability(id),
    onSuccess: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ["capabilities"] })
    },
  })

  if (isLoading) return <Spinner />

  return (
    <div>
      {data?.map(cap => (
        <CapabilityCard
          key={cap.id}
          capability={cap}
          onTrack={() => trackCapability(cap.id)}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Form Handling
- Use TanStack React Form for complex forms
- Use Server Actions for form submissions
- Implement Zod validation schemas
- Show loading states during submission
- Display error messages clearly

Example:
```typescript
import { useForm } from "@tanstack/react-form"

export function CapabilityForm() {
  const form = useForm({
    defaultValues: {
      title: "",
      description: "",
    },
    onSubmit: async ({ value }) => {
      const result = await createCapability(value)
      if (result.success) {
        toast.success("Capability created!")
      }
    },
  })

  return (
    <form onSubmit={(e) => {
      e.preventDefault()
      form.handleSubmit()
    }}>
      {/* form fields */}
    </form>
  )
}
```

## shadcn/ui Components
- Install via: `npx shadcn@latest add [component]`
- Located in `/src/components/ui/`
- Customize as needed (they're copied to your project)
- Use `cn()` utility for conditional className merging
- Follow the "new-york" style variant

Example:
```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

export function CustomButton({ className, ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <Button
      className={cn("custom-styles", className)}
      {...props}
    />
  )
}
```

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide alt text for images
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Use ARIA labels when needed (but prefer semantic HTML)
- Maintain color contrast ratios (WCAG AA)

Example:
```typescript
<button
  type="button"
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  aria-pressed={isOpen}
  onClick={handleClose}
>
  <X className="h-4 w-4" />
</button>
```

## Performance Optimization
- Use `React.memo` for expensive pure components
- Use `useMemo` for expensive calculations
- Use `useCallback` for callbacks passed to memoized children
- Avoid anonymous functions in JSX when possible for memoized components

Example:
```typescript
import { memo, useMemo, useCallback } from "react"

export const ExpensiveList = memo(function ExpensiveList({ items, onItemClick }) {
  const sortedItems = useMemo(() => {
    return items.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name))
  }, [items])

  const handleClick = useCallback((id: string) => {
    onItemClick(id)
  }, [onItemClick])

  return (
    <div>
      {sortedItems.map(item => (
        <Item key={item.id} item={item} onClick={handleClick} />
      ))}
    </div>
  )
})
```

## Error Boundaries
- Wrap components in error boundaries
- Provide fallback UI for errors
- Log errors appropriately

Example:
```typescript
"use client"

import { Component, type ReactNode } from "react"

interface Props {
  children: ReactNode
  fallback?: ReactNode
}

export class ErrorBoundary extends Component<Props, { hasError: boolean }> {
  constructor(props: Props) {
    super(props)
    this.state = { hasError: false }
  }

  static getDerivedStateFromError() {
    return { hasError: true }
  }

  componentDidCatch(error: Error) {
    console.error("Error boundary caught:", error)
  }

  render() {
    if (this.state.hasError) {
      return this.props.fallback || <div>Something went wrong</div>
    }

    return this.props.children
  }
}
```
